WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.704
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.572
Marques:
The original Walkman has been

00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:08.374
an outdated piece of tech
for a while now,

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:10.343
but the movie
"Guardians of the Galaxy"

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.345
<i> released in 2014,</i>

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:13.813
<i> sort of brought the nostalgia</i>

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.681
of the original Walkman back.

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.184 line:8%
<i> In that film, Chris Pratt's
 character Peter Quill</i>

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:20.787
had one cassette tape
in one Walkman

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.689
through 26 years in space.

00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:27.493
It can be as low as 455 degrees
below zero Fahrenheit

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:29.529
in the coldest parts of space.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.397
That seems like it would be
problematic for the Walkman.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.299
So today I want to
try to answer the question

00:00:33.332 --> 00:00:35.568
would that Walkman
and that cassette

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.103
and that pair of headphones

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:40.073
have lasted
for those 26 years?

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.809
So, to test it, out I've brought
a tub of liquid nitrogen.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:46.712
But I'm not exactly qualified
to handle liquid nitrogen,

00:00:46.745 --> 00:00:50.083
- so, of course we have
  our safety instructor.
- Hi. Nice to see you.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.618 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
So, liquid nitrogen.
It's super, super cold.

00:00:52.651 --> 00:00:55.688 align:start size:81% position:19%
So, to protect Cryo-Apron,
gloves,

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.390 align:start size:75% position:25%
and some safety glasses.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.525 align:start position:0%
All right,
I feel really safe.
How do I look?

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:01.761 align:start size:97% position:3%
- A little high school
  science-y, but that's okay.
- Perfect.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:03.496 align:start size:63% position:38%
So, I'm gonna grab
the liquid nitrogen.

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:06.466
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.800
And it looks just like water.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.602
It's just an awful lot colder.

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:14.674
It boils at about minus 300
and some odd degrees Fahrenheit.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.342 align:start position:0%
So I'm gonna start off
with the cassette tape.

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.244
So, let's pretend this is
"Awesome Mix Vol. 1."

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:20.279 size:81% position:41%
And we'll go ahead and see

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.648
if it would've survived
the cold.

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:23.850
( clicking )

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.219 align:start position:0%
That's a strange sound.

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:32.292
All right, so we've frozen
the cassette tape.

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:35.394 align:start position:0%
Headphones next.

00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:39.866
( crackling )

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.803 align:start position:0%
Liquid nitrogen,
meet battery.

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:50.343 align:start size:81% position:19%
One more for good measure.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.512 size:84% position:42%
And what you're seeing off
the outside of that battery

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.714 align:start size:69% position:31%
is all of the moisture
in the air,

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.416 align:start size:53% position:47%
just like a cloud
in the sky.

00:01:57.449 --> 00:01:59.486
So, the entire Walkman
is the only thing left.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.626 align:start size:84% position:16%
- ( crackling )
- I can hear a lot
  of things happening.

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.834 align:start position:0%
Okay, see what happened
to the Walkman.

00:02:17.836 --> 00:02:20.640 align:start position:0%
Still physically intact.
You know what didn't survive

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:23.442 size:88% position:56%
is this little window here.
Brittle enough to break off.

00:02:23.475 --> 00:02:24.777 align:start position:0%
So, this is
the moment of truth

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.579 align:start size:63% position:38%
to find out
if it keeps working.

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:88% position:13%
- ( screeching )
-<i> ( high-pitched whine )</i>

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.719 align:start position:0%
Okay, that's not
"Awesome Mix Vol. 1."

00:02:33.752 --> 00:02:35.955 align:start position:0%
Fast-forward a little.

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:38.791
- ( screeching )
- You guys are--

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:41.394 align:start position:0%
You're hearing this, right?
This is pretty loud.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.595 align:start position:0%
But the wheels
aren't spinning.

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:44.564 align:start size:78% position:22%
Something about the motor

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.432 align:start position:0%
is not quite getting
enough power

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:48.434 align:start size:81% position:19%
to move the cassette tape.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
Take something down that cold,
you're gonna have problems.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:52.405
I'll say "Awesome Mix Vol. 1"

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.340 size:78% position:61%
would probably not have
actually played in space.

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:56.342 align:start position:0%
A Walkman is still awesome,
but maybe--

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:58.378 align:start position:0%
